    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "Core retains; TypeScript interprets.\n\nSource bytes, revision and project transactions, six cache handles, and request/session retention move to core. Language algorithms stay in TypeScript. Selection and failure boundaries are preserved.\n\nFollow this boundary ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#m-state",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "The CLI supplies a host module.\n\nSyntax and canonical paths belong to CLI. Daemon loads the supplied executor URL and moves ordered bytes. Renderer formats lifecycle reports; telemetry keeps usage. Node-free declarations still lead to a Node runtime.\n\nFollow this boundary ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#m-host",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "Identity crosses every boundary.\n\nCommandName travels beside argv; protocol generation advances to 5. Closed failure vocabularies and ordered guards own retry meaning: authenticate → ready → memory → queue → duplicate.\n\nFollow this boundary ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#m-identity",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "Accepted work stays accepted.\n\nCodec, validator, socket directions, lifecycle, execution, receiver and capture split apart. FIFO accepts once. Duplicate requests attach. Fetch and reattachment have independent budgets; append precedes offset advancement.\n\nFollow this boundary ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#m-delivery",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "Policy owns limits; sessions own lifetimes.\n\nOne daemon snapshot covers output, memory, retries, polling, diagnostics and deadlines. No user threshold knobs. Worker generations, sampled activity, clocks, registry identity and delivery barriers have explicit owners. Host-side policy is separate.\n\nFollow this boundary ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#m-policy",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "A staged move becomes active.\n\n#148 creates package machinery and freezes CLI copies; #149 switches the CLI and removes them. Public testing becomes read-only; compiler inventories enforce the boundary. Test and scope changes, plus eight deferred behaviors, belong in the review.\n\nFollow this boundary ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#m-cutover",
      "type": null
    },
