    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "UNEXPLAINED\nRelax test timing: executor 15 s; transfer 20 → 60 s\n\nCommit 323888b8d adds explicit 15,000 ms limits to two executor tests; 4e0dc1978 increases the twelve-MiB transport test from 20,000 to 60,000 ms. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "STATED\nPoll matching startup ownership; status test 15 → 30 s\n\nCommit b0a6ce67e says ‘Stabilize daemon startup ownership oracle’. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "UNEXPLAINED\nChoose a 30 s startup test budget\n\nThe stabilization commit explains the purpose of polling but not why the enclosing status test receives 30 seconds instead of its previous 15. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "UNEXPLAINED\nRemove 7 CLI status + 3 CLI stop scenarios\n\nCommit 9284116a4 removes seven named status cases and three named stop cases from the CLI e2e files. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "UNEXPLAINED\nDrop a completion-file wait; observe telemetry after caller exit\n\nTip commit d07002357 changes the accepted-caller launch to node --import tsx and removes the explicit completion-file wait. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "STATED\nDaemon owns clocks + registry lock identity\n\nThe architecture spec explicitly assigns daemon wall and monotonic clocks and one lock-ownership check to the daemon. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "STATED\nFinal public surface removes policy serialization + test factory\n\nThe final policy record says serialization is package-internal and test factories are package-local. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "UNEXPLAINED\nCLI executor constructs its own default policy\n\nThe daemon process and worker propagate the complete injected snapshot. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "STATED\nNode-free declarations; Node still runs the implementation\n\nPR #148 states that the dynamic runtime protects host declarations from Node ambient dependencies. Read reason and evidence ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
